 运行中的 job 行还带一个两击式停止控件：首击武装，三秒内的确认击调用 `ctx.jobs.kill`，行状态经名册流收敛（先 `stopping`，再入已结束分组，其 detail 携带 `cancelled by the user`）。该 kill 不在模型的播报台账里认领任何东西，任务的 owner agent 因此照常收到标准完成通知——模型被明确告知用户停止了它的任务，而不是留给它去猜（[参考](../../jobs/tool-jobs/README.zh.md)）。已结束分组在有进行中工作时折叠在其计数之后，并可在客户端清空。
+
+带有 `canComplete: true` 的运行中任务还显示“完成”按钮。点击后通过 `ctx.jobs.complete` 请求完成，按钮保持禁用，直到权威任务列表报告结算。请求失败时保留任务行并允许重试。此能力由生产方提供，普通任务不会额外显示完成按钮。所属 agent 通过原有任务通知流程接收生产方提供的完成消息。

 ### 展开的面板

--- a/packages/jobs/jobs/README.md
+++ b/packages/jobs/jobs/README.md
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@
 A producer streams output by naming pull sources on its spec — non-consuming offset readers the registry pumps at its own cadence — or by pushing chunks through the `JobHandle` its starter receives; both land in the job's bounded ring, where `stdout` and `stderr` chunks reach the model and `log` chunks reach observers only. Observers read retained chunks at absolute byte offsets and are signaled on advancement; the settlement that ends the job also ends the stream, and `updateProgress` publishes a live progress line into every projection until then. Observation is invisible to the model: `readAt` consumes nothing and never touches notice state.

 The shipped provider also records owned-job lifecycle metadata in the Session. Producers attach `JobSpec.toolCall` when a tool creates the job, preserving nested and root call identity. See the [durable event fields](../../../docs/subsystems/jobs.md#session-lifecycle-records) for timing and restart semantics.
+
+A producer can opt in to human completion with `JobHooks.complete()`. While that job is running, its projection carries `canComplete: true`. `complete(id, caller)` applies the same owner check as cancellation, rejects unsupported or stopping jobs, and invokes the producer hook; only the existing `done` promise commits the terminal result and notification. The hook must be synchronous and idempotent. A terminal job returns `already-finished` without changing its result.

